      "message": "Your answer, **“am used to living,” is grammatically correct**:\n\n- **“I am used to living in Tokyo”** means living there feels familiar or normal to me now.\n- **“I used to live in Tokyo”** means I lived there in the past, usually implying I no longer do.\n\nThe question asked only for a **grammatically correct completion**, without specifying the intended meaning. Both choices fit, so marking yours incorrect isn’t justified by the wording. The note also explicitly says both expressions are grammatical.",
